# Task profiles — example.
# Copy to ~/.config/kontor/profiles.conf and edit.
#
#   profile <name>  <large model>  <small model>  "<what kind of work this is>"
#
# The profile names the KIND of work. The models are what that kind implies.
# Model names must be <provider>/<model> exactly as the branch's generated
# crush.json declares them, because `kontor use` checks against that file.
#
# Deliberately not automatic: deciding "is this a cheap task?" requires
# understanding the task, which means a model call, which costs more than the
# cheap task saves. The judgement stays with the person, at the moment they
# start, which is the only place it is free.
#
# The small model is used constantly by the runner for titles and summaries.
# Keeping it cheap matters more than it looks.
#
# The `ollama/` prefix is load-bearing: `kontor use` refuses to make anything
# else the default of a branch listed as local-first. A hosted model there is
# a per-session decision, not a setting.

profile filing    ollama/small-local     ollama/small-local   "Filing, renaming, recording. No judgement required."
profile reading   ollama/large-local     ollama/small-local   "Search and summarise, locally. Nothing leaves the machine."
profile drafting  hosted/cheap-model     hosted/cheap-model   "Drafts and correspondence. Cheap hosted tier."
profile analysis  hosted/strong-model    hosted/cheap-model   "Hard work. Expensive, chosen deliberately."
